Just completed my first priest quest! For Psmith the chaotic priest,
carrying Stormbringer, it was quite a breeze. Initially I thought the
large numbers of weak monsters was dreadfully tedious, but the message
you get when you finally dispose of your nemesis is a real hoot, and
well worth the trip.

Couple of points: the Arch Priest told me that it would be easier to
defeat my nemesis in the daytime? Is this true? The program actually
calls date() or something and accordingly modifies the luck of some,
shall we say, creatures of the night?

This leads to some interesting possibilities:

Seasons: get time of year from date() and location from hostname() (the
YouAreHere Web server at SUNY Buffalo has code for doing that).

High latitudes in winter: it's chilly in the dungeon and you freeze your
butt, esp if you're wearing only a Hawaiian shirt. Burns up your food
faster. Of course, cold resistance changes all that.

Low lat, summer: wearing more than a Hawaiian shirt makes you sweat,
gives you BO. Your best friends won't tell you, and pets and monsters
will flee from your vicinity. But insect and bees will buzz around you
constantly.

Call hosttype() or equivalent to find your operating system. If it says
DOS, you stand revealed as a despicable member of that caste of wretched
untouchables, the PCheads! Start with Int of 3 and Wis of 0, no matter
what the class.
